From 01a77dab8c4cf23d1e49273fa3c88bb0bb4fc887 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AIwork4me <AIwork4me@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:37:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] MIOpen: keep RTC type traits self-contained when no host
 STL is reachable

Runtime-compiled MIOpen kernels failed on environments whose HIPRTC
toolchain cannot resolve a host C++ standard library - notably AMD's
Windows pip wheels, whose msvc-triple clang ships no stdlib and no
include-path configuration (MIOpen#3956; also seen in AMD's own Windows
release CI, TheRock#8292). Since 'All 7.0 hipRTC fixes' (#3803) wrapped
miopen_type_traits.hpp - and 'use utility if hip version > 7.0' (#3147)
independently wrapped miopen_utility.hpp - the internal no-STL
compatibility shims are disabled for HIP >= 7 and the real headers are
included even in runtime-compile mode.

Prefer the real headers whenever they are reachable (__has_include) so
STL-present environments keep byte-identical behavior, and fall back to
new self-tested freestanding definitions only where no standard library
resolves - the state in which compilation previously always failed.
Deliberately partial standard libraries (one header reachable, the other
not) are rejected loudly instead of risking redefinitions. The HIP < 7
legacy shim arms are left unchanged. The new headers are registered in
the embedded-kernel include list.
